Subject: Tweak: replays skip the parts of cutscenes their players skipped
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A cutscene is no part of the fixed steps: the match stands still while it
plays (FixedUpdateTask steps only in TASK_GAMEPLAY; a network match stops at
the step where every machine said its cutscene was loaded), on each machine
for as long as it lasts there. A player who skips a part the presentation's
script marks (BeginByPass to EndByPass, numbered from 0 in each game by
mByPassNumber) tells the other machine with NetMessageSkipNis, outside the
steps. So a replay, or a match watched live, played every cutscene in full:
it fell behind the players and raced through the next play to catch up.

The port notes each press that counts for a part and how far into it
(mscharged_tweak_presentation_pressed, made here or on the other machine),
keeps that in the replay and sends it beside the live stream. A replay presses
in the same parts as far into them, the way a press from another machine
counts (mSkipPastByPass, which sends nothing), so the game's own rules decide
the rest as they did for the players: a score that still counts holds the
skip. The viewer's own presses still count. RECHARGED_TEST_CUTSCENE_SKIP=
<seconds> presses for the local player in every part, for tests of the
players' side, only where DetectSkipPress would take a press of that player's
pad.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_replay.h b/include/mscharged_replay.h
index 4b66d91..86c87d4 100644
--- a/include/mscharged_replay.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_replay.h
@@ -51,6 +51,21 @@ void mscharged_tweak_replay_start_match(void);
 // After the loading chose the difficulty: a recorded match notes it, a replay
 // sets the recorded one again.
 void mscharged_tweak_replay_difficulty(void);
+// Cutscenes (tweak patch 0072): a cutscene is no part of the steps, the
+// match stands still while it plays, so a replay presses skip in the parts of
+// them where its players did, as far into them. Presentation::Update, at each
+// update that is not paused: whether `inside` a part a player may skip, its
+// number in the game (the bypass number) and the update's time; whether to
+// press now, as its players did.
+bool mscharged_tweak_presentation_skip(bool inside, int part, float deltaT);
+// Where a player's press would count (DetectSkipPress, for a pad that may
+// skip): whether the local player presses now, in a match, for a test of the
+// players' side (RECHARGED_TEST_CUTSCENE_SKIP=<seconds> into each part).
+bool mscharged_tweak_presentation_test_press(void);
+// A press counts for part `part` now, made here or on another machine of a
+// network match (the game skips the part once nothing holds it: a score that
+// still counts); at each update until the part ends.
+void mscharged_tweak_presentation_pressed(int part);
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
